# Current theses

## Thesis T-migrated-adapters-maven: Preserve reviewed project guidance
Status: accepted
Based-on: user-reviewed-contract-migration

### Guidance
#### module Maven checkout integration

Detect root `pom.xml` and consume Maven exports whose name is `group:artifact`. `Export.Path` is
the consumer-root-relative POM or module directory in the one submodule checkout. This adapter
does not clone, copy, or own that checkout.

#### decision Generated reactor plus precise root POM blocks

The wholly owned `deps/git-a2a.maven/pom.xml` is a sorted aggregator of checkout module paths.
The consumer POM receives one marked aggregator module and one marked dependency per dependency;
existing XML outside markers stays byte-identical. Tool-created empty containers are removed.

#### invariant Reactor versions must match

The managed dependency uses `${project.version}` because Maven composite substitution does not
exist. The consumer reactor and component artifact must publish the same version. Read-only
Capability requires a Maven `group:artifact` coordinate and a relative non-escaping checkout
path. Pull verifies the checked-out module, writes the reactor integration, and runs Maven
`validate` so the resolved project reference is usable without compiling the application.
Remove validates the remaining reactor after deleting only owned integration; Inspect reports a
missing module or POM.

#### test Golden lifecycle

Tests cover existing containers, read-only capability and coordinate validation, private editor
idempotence, repair, Inspect, byte-restoring removal, sorted ownership, and missing modules.

### Rationale
Migrated from the pre-2.0 HINT source format without changing its guidance.

